# =============================================================================
# THIS FILE IS A SECURITY CONTROL, NOT AN OPTIMISATION.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. A `git add -A` here was one command away from
# committing three private cosign signing keys, a 1,014-file Python virtualenv,
# and seven editor lock files to a public GitHub repo. The keys were untracked
# but NOT ignored, which is the dangerous combination: invisible in `git status`
# summaries, swept up by any bulk add.
#
# Verified 2026-07-27. Deny by default; allow explicitly.
# =============================================================================

# --- Signing keys and credentials --------------------------------------------
# Nothing that can sign, authenticate, or decrypt belongs in git. A committed
# key is compromised the moment it is pushed, and rewriting history does not
# un-compromise it - the only remedy is rotation.
# CIS Docker 4.10 | PCI-DSS 8.3.1 | NIST IA-5
*.key
cosign.key
!cosign.pub
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
*.ppk

# Tokens, PATs, and anything that looks like one
env/
*token*
*.pat
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Cloud and cluster credentials
.aws/
.azure/
.gcloud/
.kube/config
kubeconfig*

# --- Language and tool caches ------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
.npm/
vendor/
target/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
# LibreOffice writes .~lock.<name># next to any open document.
.~lock.*#
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.direnv/

# --- Pipeline evidence -------------------------------------------------------
# Evidence is staged locally then shipped to WORM storage. It must not live in
# git: history is rewritable by anyone with force-push, which is precisely the
# property evidence retention has to exclude. SOX, FedRAMP AU-11.
**/evidence/**
!**/evidence/.gitkeep

# Scan output and SBOMs regenerated on every run
trivy-report.json
*.sbom.json

# --- Large build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------
container-from-scratch/rootfs/
container-from-scratch/rootfs.tar.gz
*.tar.gz
!**/testdata/**/*.tar.gz

# NOTE: two compiled binaries are currently untracked and NOT ignored:
#   hardened-oci/oras-learning-with-project/image-from-scratch/app         (~7 MB)
#   hardened-oci/oras-learning-with-project/image-from-scratch/scratch-api (~5 MB)
# Left alone deliberately - for a build-from-scratch exercise the static binary
# may be the artifact under study. Decide whether they belong in git before any
# bulk add; if not, add them here.
